        "title": "Pharmacogenomics and Personalized Medicine",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Pharmacogenomics (PGx) is the study of how genetic variation affects drug response. It explains why the same drug and dose causes therapeutic success in one patient, toxicity in another, and no effect in a third. Personalized (precision) medicine uses genetic, genomic, and other molecular data to select the right drug at the right dose."
